oments  and i loved in particular when vision  was first doing his neighborhood watch  and he notices that woman  hanging up halloween decorations outside  she's just going like this i love that  the director side to hang on that shot  because that's what made it creepy  because it just kept going and she's  crying  really eerie and it goes to vision now  seeing all these people  at the edge of west view now just  stopped they're not  moving and it has that westworld feel to  it  leading to a great scene where he finds  agnes now  now remember a lot of people think agnes  is the character from the comics agatha  who's a witch who kind of  shows scarlet witch her powers but look  she's dressed like a witch  she's got the gray hair it might be a  red herring but it's interesting they  let her do that  which like laugh in her not brainwashed  state so i really do believe  we'll see that she was the one kind of  helping scarlet witch learn more about  how powerful she actually is and that  she probably is a victim too but was  kind of part of this mess that got her  and wanda in this trap whoever the big  power is using wanda's big power or  maybe just  influencing her that's what's so  effective too you're constantly  wondering like  how much of an antagonist is wanda in  this show in this story because we see  at the end she uses her powers  to bring that hex further but who was  really the influence behind her is  someone influencing her mind  don't really fully know they do a good  job of keeping mystery throughout while  they're still giving us answers  and the tone here there's still so much  creepy stuff going on  this 90s kids commercial which really  nails  those type of commercials are all over  the place watching that as kids  and it's this yogurt commercial for yo  magic and also this big moment where  like when wanda saw vision in this dead  body  version it was even scarier seeing  pietro in his  the body that was killed by ultron and  that she's just  usi